---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /
title: I own every gate between a change and a real person
shortTitle: Libin Samkutty
description: Senior QA Automation Engineer. I own the test infrastructure, release gates, data platform and AI evaluation systems for a digital health platform.
bodyClass: home
---
<section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__inner">
        <div class="hero__content">
            <p class="hero__eyebrow">{{ site.title }} · {{ site.location.city }}, {{ site.location.country }}</p>

            <h1 class="hero__title">{{ site.plainClaim }}</h1>

            <p class="hero__lede">
                Sole QA on a digital health platform in {% metric "countries" %} countries. I own the
                test infrastructure, the release gates and the data pipeline behind the dashboards.
                The hardest of those is deciding, on evidence, whether a generated medical answer is
                safe to send to someone who will act on it.
            </p>

            <p class="hero__actions">
                <a class="button button--primary" href="{{ '/work/' | url }}">See the work</a>
                <a class="button button--ghost" href="{{ '/resume/' | url }}">Résumé</a>
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__portrait">
            {# Alt is the person's name. A portrait's alt text is who it is, not a
               description of the suit. Eager and high priority because this is the
               LCP element — and for the same reason it gets no reveal animation. #}
            {% image "headshot.png", site.name, "(min-width: 64em) 480px, 60vw", { eager: true, class: "hero__image" } %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

{# The first thing below the hero is the surface owned, not a figure. A reader
   deciding in seven seconds needs to place the scope; the numbers that qualify
   it live in the case studies, where they have room to carry their provenance.
   `.evidence` is unchanged and still rendered on /styleguide/. #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="own-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="own-title">What I own</h2>

        <div class="definition-list definition-list--columns">
            {% for item in projects.whatIOwn %}
            <div class="definition-list__item" data-reveal>
                <h3 class="definition-list__term">{{ item.title }}</h3>
                <p class="definition-list__description">{{ item.body }}</p>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="work-title">Selected work</h2>

        <ul class="card-list card-list--three">
            {% for item in collections.caseStudies %}
                {% if item.fileSlug in projects.featuredCaseStudies %}
                <li class="card card--case-study{% if item.data.flagship %} card--flagship{% endif %}" data-reveal>
                    <p class="card__eyebrow">
                        <span>{{ item.data.period }}</span>
                        {% if item.data.flagship %}<span class="card__flag">Start here</span>{% endif %}
                    </p>
                    <h3 class="card__title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></h3>
                    {% if item.data.outcome %}<p class="card__outcome">{{ item.data.outcome }}</p>{% endif %}
                    <p class="card__body">{{ item.data.description }}</p>
                    <ul class="chips">
                        {% for tech in item.data.stack | limit(4) %}<li class="chip">{{ tech }}</li>{% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                </li>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>

        <p class="section__more"><a href="{{ '/work/' | url }}">All work, including the systems that didn't warrant a case study</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--emphasis" aria-labelledby="wrong-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="wrong-title">Things that didn't work</h2>

        {# Two, not four. `.callout-grid` is two columns at 60em, so three leaves
           a hole, and article.css warns against more than two limitation
           callouts in a viewport. These two also link to the case studies the
           cards above leave out, so five of six are one click from here. #}
        <div class="callout-grid">
            <div class="callout callout--limitation">
                <h3 class="callout__title">I built an evaluation system that could not fail</h3>
                <p>
                    The platform's first LLM-as-a-judge used the same model family that had generated
                    the answers it was grading. It scored well. It scored well because a model asked to
                    grade its own reasoning agrees with itself. That is not an independent check. It is
                    closer to a mirror.
                </p>
                <p><a href="{{ '/work/llm-judge-independence/' | url }}">How I found it and what replaced it</a></p>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 class="callout__title">Four testing layers all missed the same gap</h3>
                <p>
                    Golden-dataset regression, the conversational suite, retrieval faithfulness scoring
                    and manual spot-checks were all green while a class of clinically important query
                    was getting a sympathetic non-answer. Every layer was testing what we had thought to
                    write down. None of them was reading what users were actually sending.
                </p>
                <p><a href="{{ '/work/production-evaluation-pipeline/' | url }}">What the production pipeline caught</a></p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="writing-title">Latest writing</h2>

        <ul class="card-list card-list--three">
            {% for item in collections.posts | limit(3) %}
            <li class="card card--post" data-reveal>
                <p class="card__eyebrow"><time datetime="{{ item.date | isoDate }}">{{ item.date | readableDate }}</time></p>
                <h3 class="card__title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></h3>
                <p class="card__body">{{ item.data.description }}</p>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>

        <p class="section__more"><a href="{{ '/writing/' | url }}">All writing</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="timeline-title">Where I've been</h2>

        <ol class="timeline">
            {% for marker in timeline.markers %}
            <li class="timeline__item{% if loop.last %} timeline__item--current{% endif %}">
                <p class="timeline__period">
                    <time datetime="{{ marker.date | isoDate }}">{{ marker.date | monthYear }}</time>
                </p>
                <h3 class="timeline__title">{{ marker.label }}</h3>
                {% if marker.detail %}<p class="timeline__org">{{ marker.detail }}</p>{% endif %}
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ol>

        <p class="section__more"><a href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">The longer version</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--cta" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
    <div class="wrap wrap--measure">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="cta-title">Currently open to senior and lead quality roles</h2>
        <p>
            {{ site.targetRoles | join(", ") }}. I own quality end to end, and the sharpest version
            of that problem right now is AI evaluation. If a wrong answer has a cost in your
            product, that is the work I want.
        </p>
        <p class="button-row">
            <a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email me</a>
            <a class="button button--ghost" href="{{ site.profiles.linkedin }}" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
